IMPORT prelude

-- Strata Titles Act 1985 (Western Australia) -- what a lot owner owes the strata company and when it can charge interest
-- (ss 14(8), 37(1), 100, 102), who casts the lot's vote and what a special resolution is (ss 120(2), 123(4)-(6), 126),
-- what the by-laws can and cannot do to the owner (ss 44(2), 45(2), 46, 47), what the owner is told and may do when
-- buying a lot, off the plan or not (ss 110, 156-164, the s 3(1) notifiable variations), and how the owner takes a
-- dispute to the Tribunal and seeks review of its order (ss 83, 197, 210).
--
-- SEAT: the owner of a lot in a strata titles scheme (and, before settlement, the buyer who is about to become one).
-- Every decision is phrased as the owner would ask it: "How much is my contribution", "Can my lot's vote be cast",
-- "Is this by-law invalid", "May I avoid my contract", "Can I take this to the Tribunal".
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3(1) (type 1 and type 2 notifiable variation, working day), s 14(8), s 37(1), s 44(2), s 45(2),
-- s 46(a)-(c), (e)-(j), s 47(1), (2), (4), (6), s 83, s 100(1)(c), (2), (4)(b), (6), (7), s 102(5), (6), s 107(2), (4),
-- s 110(1)-(3), s 120(2), s 123(4)-(6), s 126, s 156(3)-(4), s 157(3), s 158, s 159, s 160, s 161, s 162, s 163,
-- s 164(2), s 197(1)(a), (h), (3), s 210(1)-(2).
--
-- Edition: the compilation with editorial changes as at 26 June 2025 (last amendment in operation: Transfer of Land
-- Amendment Act 2022, 7 August 2023), legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc_48587, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48587.txt (retrieved 7 September 2026). Regulations used: Strata Titles (General)
-- Regulations 2019, version 00-w0-00, in currency from 20 August 2026, mrdoc_49798, deposited at
-- ../../../strata-titles-general-regulations-2019/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49798.txt (retrieved 19 October 2026):
-- regs 58 (by-law penalty $2 000), 78 (interest 11% a year), 79 (designated strata company over $5 000 000), 80 and 81
-- ($500 a lot), 82 (two quotations), 86 (certificate fee $140, plus 10% with GST) and 162 (internal review).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: planning, scheme plans and registration (Parts 2-5), the scheme developer's duties (Part 6) except as they
-- reach the buyer through s 156(4), structural alterations (Part 7 Div 2), insurance (ss 84, 97-99), meetings, councils
-- and strata managers (ss 127-155), ordinary resolutions and resolutions without dissent as counted (s 123(1)-(3), (7)),
-- leasehold schemes, survey-strata specifics, the content of the default by-laws (Schedules 1 and 2), Part 11
-- variation, Part 12 termination, the Tribunal's orders in detail (ss 199-209) and interest after a change of owner.
-- Machinery out: ss 1-2, 4-5, 218-228 and the Schedules of transitional provisions.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Strata Titles Act 1985 -- the lot owner's questions`

§§ `the numbers the regulations set`

-- reg 78: "For the purposes of section 100(4)(b), the rate of simple interest specified is 11% per annum."
`the regulated interest rate` MEANS 11%

-- reg 79(1): a designated strata company includes one for "a strata scheme that has a scheme building replacement cost of
-- more than $5 000 000" or a survey-strata scheme whose common property improvements cost more than that to replace.
`the replacement cost threshold` MEANS 5000000

-- reg 80(1): the s 102(5) amount is "the number of lots in the strata titles scheme by $500". reg 81: the s 102(6)(a)(ii)
-- amount "is $500 (being $500 for each lot in the strata titles scheme)".
`the regulated amount per lot` MEANS 500

-- reg 58: "the maximum amount that may be imposed by the Tribunal by way of penalty for contravention of scheme by-laws is
-- $2 000." s 47(6)(d): "a daily penalty may be imposed for a continuing contravention only if that is authorised by the
-- regulations". No regulation in the deposited version mentions a daily penalty (searched for "daily", "each day" and
-- "per day").
`the regulated by-law penalty` MEANS 2000

-- reg 86(1)(c), (d): the maximum fee for a s 110 certificate is $140 for either kind; (3): "increased by 10% if the strata
-- company is required to remit GST".
`the regulated certificate fee` MEANS 140

§§ `ss 14(8), 37(1), 100 -- contributions to the funds`

-- s 14(8): the strata company "is comprised of the owners for the time being of the lots" -- the owner is a member.
-- s 37(1): the schedule of unit entitlements allocates "a whole number (a unit entitlement) to each lot" and states their
-- sum. Its note: the unit entitlement determines the owner's share of the common property, "subject to the scheme
-- bylaws, the contributions payable by the owner", and the vote.
DECLARE `Fund` IS ONE OF
    `the administrative fund`   -- s 100(1)(a): "for administrative expenses", insurance and the company's other obligations
    `the reserve fund`          -- s 100(2)(a): "to meet contingent expenses, other than those of a routine nature, and other major expenses"

-- s 100(1)(c): the administrative fund is raised "by levying contributions on owners of lots -- (i) in proportion to the
-- unit entitlements of their respective lots; or (ii) if the scheme bylaws provide for a different basis for levying
-- contributions, in accordance with that basis". s 100(2)(c): the reserve fund is raised "in proportion to the unit
-- entitlements of their respective lots" -- with no by-law alternative.
@export How much must I pay as my lot's share of a levy my strata company has raised for its administrative fund or reserve fund (s 100(1)(c), (2)(c))?
GIVEN `the fund` IS A `Fund` @desc Which fund the levy is for: the administrative fund or the reserve fund
      `the amount the strata company resolved to raise` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount, in dollars, the strata company resolved to raise from all the lots
      `my lot's unit entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit entitlement of your lot, from the schedule of unit entitlements
      `the sum of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all the lots in the scheme
      `the by-laws provide a different basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme by-laws set a basis for contributions other than unit entitlement
      `my share under the by-law basis` IS A NUMBER @desc If the by-laws set a different basis: your lot's share under it, as a fraction (for example 0.05); otherwise 0
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my contribution` IS
    CONSIDER `the fund`
    WHEN `the administrative fund` THEN
        IF `the by-laws provide a different basis`
        THEN `the amount the strata company resolved to raise` TIMES `my share under the by-law basis`
        ELSE `the amount the strata company resolved to raise` TIMES `my lot's unit entitlement` DIVIDED BY `the sum of the unit entitlements`
    WHEN `the reserve fund` THEN
        `the amount the strata company resolved to raise` TIMES `my lot's unit entitlement` DIVIDED BY `the sum of the unit entitlements`

-- s 100(2): a strata company "must, if it is a designated strata company, and may, in any other case" establish a reserve
-- fund. (2A): a designated strata company must have a 10 year plan, revised at least once in each 5 years. (7):
-- "designated strata company means -- (a) a strata company for a scheme with 10 or more lots; or (b) a strata company
-- included in this definition by the regulations" -- reg 79, above.
@export Must my strata company keep a reserve fund and a 10 year plan, so that I will be levied for it (s 100(2), (2A), (7); reg 79)?
GIVEN `the number of lots in the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots there are in the strata titles scheme
      `the replacement cost` IS A NUMBER @desc The replacement cost, in dollars, of the scheme building (strata scheme) or of the improvements on the common property (survey-strata scheme)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my strata company keep a reserve fund` IF
        `the number of lots in the scheme` AT LEAST 10
    OR  `the replacement cost` GREATER THAN `the replacement cost threshold`

-- s 100(4): a contribution "(b) if not paid when it becomes due and payable, bears interest on the amount unpaid at the rate
-- of simple interest specified in the regulations, unless the company determines (either generally or in a particular
-- case) that an unpaid contribution bears no interest or interest at a lesser rate". The rate is a year's rate; the
-- encoder counts it by days over a 365-day year (an inference: the Act and reg 78 do not say how a part-year is counted).
@export How much interest can my strata company charge me on a contribution I paid late (s 100(4)(b); reg 78)?
GIVEN `the amount unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the contribution, in dollars, left unpaid after it fell due
      `the days it was overdue` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from the due date until it was paid
      `the company has determined a lesser rate or none` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company has resolved that unpaid contributions bear no interest or a lower rate
      `the rate the company determined` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that yearly rate as a fraction (for example 0.05 for 5%, or 0 for no interest); otherwise 0
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much interest do I owe` IS
    `the amount unpaid` TIMES `the rate that applies` TIMES `the days it was overdue` DIVIDED BY 365
    WHERE
        `the rate that applies` MEANS
            IF `the company has determined a lesser rate or none` AND `the rate the company determined` LESS THAN `the regulated interest rate`
            THEN `the rate the company determined`
            ELSE `the regulated interest rate`

-- s 100(6): "The owner of a lot is liable in respect of any contribution levied under this section and any interest on the
-- contribution, jointly and severally with any person who was liable to pay that contribution and interest when that owner
-- became the owner of that lot, to pay so much of that contribution and interest as was unpaid when the owner became the
-- owner of that lot." s 110(3): a s 110 certificate "is conclusive evidence of the matters stated in the certificate, as at
-- the date of the certificate, in favour of a person taking an estate or interest in a lot for valuable consideration".
-- The encoder's reading of the two together: what the certificate stated as owing at its date caps what the buyer can be
-- made to pay for that period; arrears arising after its date are not covered by it.
@export Having bought my lot, how much of the previous owner's unpaid contributions and interest can the strata company make me pay (s 100(6), s 110(3))?
GIVEN `the arrears at the certificate date` IS A NUMBER @desc Contributions and interest, in dollars, actually unpaid at the date of the s 110 certificate (or at settlement, if you had no certificate)
      `the arrears arising after the certificate date` IS A NUMBER @desc Contributions and interest, in dollars, that fell unpaid after the certificate date and before you became owner (0 if no certificate)
      `I bought with a s 110 certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or your conveyancer) obtained a certificate under s 110(2) for the lot before buying it
      `the arrears the certificate stated` IS A NUMBER @desc The outstanding amount the certificate stated, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the previous owner's arrears must I pay` IS
    IF `I bought with a s 110 certificate`
    THEN `the lesser of` `the arrears at the certificate date` `the arrears the certificate stated` PLUS `the arrears arising after the certificate date`
    ELSE `the arrears at the certificate date` PLUS `the arrears arising after the certificate date`
    WHERE
        GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
        `the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `s 102 -- spending outside the budget`

-- s 102(5): a budget or variation providing for expenditure on common property under s 91(2) (improvements beyond repair,
-- "other than expenditure on sustainability infrastructure") "exceeding an amount determined under the regulations" must
-- be "approved by special resolution". reg 80(1): lots times $500.
@export Must a budget that spends on improving or altering the common property be approved by special resolution, so that my vote counts against it (s 102(5); reg 80)?
GIVEN `the improvement spending` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars the budget or variation provides for improving or altering the common property beyond repair (not sustainability infrastructure)
      `the number of lots in the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots there are in the strata titles scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the improvement budget pass by special resolution` IF
    `the improvement spending` GREATER THAN `the number of lots in the scheme` TIMES `the regulated amount per lot`

-- s 102(6): "A strata company must not make any expenditure that is not authorised by an approved budget except" (a)
-- spending in a financial year not exceeding, for each lot, the amount fixed by special resolution or else by the
-- regulations ($500, reg 81); (b) spending (not of the s 102(5) kind) after notice to owners and first mortgagees, with
-- quotations if the regulations require (reg 82: at least 2), and "within 14 days ... objection ... has not been
-- notified" by the owners or first mortgagees "of (I) 25% or more of the lots in the scheme; or (II) lots of which the
-- total unit entitlement is 25% or more"; (c) spending "required by a court or tribunal or by a notice or order given under
-- a written law".
@export Can my strata company spend money that the approved budget does not authorise, without a further vote (s 102(6); regs 81, 82)?
GIVEN `the unbudgeted spending this financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc Total dollars spent this financial year outside the approved budget, including the proposed item
      `the number of lots in the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots there are in the strata titles scheme
      `a per-lot amount was fixed by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company has fixed its own per-lot amount by special resolution
      `the per-lot amount fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that amount per lot in dollars; otherwise 0
      `it improves or alters the common property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the spending is on improving or altering the common property beyond repair (the s 102(5) kind)
      `notice and two quotations were given to owners and first mortgagees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether notice in the approved form, with at least two quotations, went to every owner and first mortgagee
      `the lots objecting within 14 days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots' owners or first mortgagees objected in writing within 14 days
      `the unit entitlement of the lots objecting` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of the lots whose owners or first mortgagees objected
      `the sum of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all the lots
      `a court, tribunal or written-law notice requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, the Tribunal or a notice or order under a written law requires the spending
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the strata company spend outside the budget` IF
        `the unbudgeted spending this financial year` AT MOST `the number of lots in the scheme` TIMES `the per-lot amount`
    OR  (    (NOT `it improves or alters the common property`)
         AND `notice and two quotations were given to owners and first mortgagees`
         AND `the lots objecting within 14 days` LESS THAN `the number of lots in the scheme` TIMES 25%
         AND `the unit entitlement of the lots objecting` LESS THAN `the sum of the unit entitlements` TIMES 25%)
    OR  `a court, tribunal or written-law notice requires it`
    WHERE
        `the per-lot amount` MEANS
            IF `a per-lot amount was fixed by special resolution`
            THEN `the per-lot amount fixed`
            ELSE `the regulated amount per lot`

§§ `ss 120, 123, 126 -- my lot's vote`

DECLARE `Kind of resolution` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary resolution`
    `a special resolution`
    `a resolution without dissent`
    `a unanimous resolution`
    `a termination resolution`
    `a resolution postponing the expiry day`

-- s 120(1): "The owner of each lot ... is entitled to 1 vote". (2): but may not cast it if "(a) the resolution is not
-- required to be a unanimous resolution or a resolution without dissent and is not a resolution for postponing the expiry
-- day for a leasehold scheme or a termination resolution; and (b) there is an outstanding amount recoverable under this
-- Act owed to the strata company by the owner of the lot".
@export Can I cast my lot's vote on this resolution even though I owe the strata company money (s 120(2))?
GIVEN `the resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution` @desc The kind of resolution being voted on
      `the amount I owe the strata company` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars you owe the strata company that are outstanding and recoverable under the Act (0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I cast my lot's vote` IF
        `the amount I owe the strata company` AT MOST 0
    OR  CONSIDER `the resolution`
        WHEN `an ordinary resolution` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a special resolution` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 126: "(a) if the lot is subject to a registered mortgage -- (i) the first mortgagee of the lot may, in person or by
-- proxy, cast the vote on behalf of the owner of the lot; and (ii) the owner may cast the vote if the first mortgagee does
-- not do so; and (b) in any event -- (i) if the owner of the lot has not attained 18 years of age, the owner may not cast
-- the vote but the owner's guardian may do so ... (iii) if there are coowners of the lot, the coowners may only cast the
-- vote through jointly appointing a single proxy (who may be 1 of the coowners)." The encoder does not combine an owner
-- under 18 with a mortgage; s 126(b)(ii) (an owner unable to control property) is not encoded.
DECLARE `Who casts my lot's vote` IS ONE OF
    `nobody, while I owe the strata company money`
    `my first mortgagee; failing it, I do, in person or by proxy`
    `my first mortgagee; failing it, my co-owners and I through one proxy we appoint jointly`
    `my guardian, because I am under 18`
    `my co-owners and I, only through one proxy we appoint jointly`
    `I do, in person or by proxy`

@export Who may cast my lot's vote on a resolution of the strata company (ss 120(2), (6), 126)?
GIVEN `the resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution` @desc The kind of resolution being voted on
      `the amount I owe the strata company` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars you owe the strata company that are outstanding and recoverable under the Act (0 if none)
      `my lot is subject to a registered mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a registered mortgage over your lot
      `I own the lot with co-owners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the lot together with someone else (for example as joint tenants)
      `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18 years old
GIVETH A `Who casts my lot's vote`
DECIDE `Who may cast my lot's vote` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Can I cast my lot's vote` `the resolution` `the amount I owe the strata company`
            THEN `nobody, while I owe the strata company money`
        IF `my lot is subject to a registered mortgage` AND `I own the lot with co-owners`
            THEN `my first mortgagee; failing it, my co-owners and I through one proxy we appoint jointly`
        IF `my lot is subject to a registered mortgage`
            THEN `my first mortgagee; failing it, I do, in person or by proxy`
        IF `I am under 18`
            THEN `my guardian, because I am under 18`
        IF `I own the lot with co-owners`
            THEN `my co-owners and I, only through one proxy we appoint jointly`
        OTHERWISE `I do, in person or by proxy`

-- s 123(4): a special resolution needs 14 days' notice and votes in favour of "not less than 50%" of the lots by number and
-- of the unit entitlements, and votes against of "less than 25%" by number and by unit entitlements. (5): "For a 2-lot
-- scheme, a resolution is only to be regarded as a special resolution if it is a unanimous resolution." (6): for a 3, 4 or
-- 5-lot scheme, in favour "not less than 2", "3" or "4" lots respectively and "not less than 50% of the unit entitlements",
-- with no limb on the votes against. s 123(1): unanimous means "the vote attached to each lot in the scheme is cast in
-- favour".
@export Did the resolution pass as a special resolution, the kind needed for a conduct by-law that binds me (s 123(4)-(6))?
GIVEN `the number of lots in the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots there are in the strata titles scheme
      `the sum of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the unit entitlements of all the lots
      `14 days' notice of its terms was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every member got 14 days' notice of the terms before voting opened
      `the lots voting for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots' votes were cast in favour
      `the unit entitlement voting for` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of the lots voting in favour
      `the lots voting against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lots' votes were cast against
      `the unit entitlement voting against` IS A NUMBER @desc The total unit entitlement of the lots voting against
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did it pass as a special resolution` IF
    `14 days' notice of its terms was given` AND `the votes suffice`
    WHERE
        `the votes suffice` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the number of lots in the scheme` AT MOST 2
                    THEN `the lots voting for` AT LEAST `the number of lots in the scheme`
                IF `the number of lots in the scheme` AT MOST 5
                    THEN     `the lots voting for` AT LEAST `the number of lots in the scheme` MINUS 1
                         AND `the unit entitlement voting for` AT LEAST `the sum of the unit entitlements` TIMES 50%
                OTHERWISE    `the lots voting for` AT LEAST `the number of lots in the scheme` TIMES 50%
                         AND `the unit entitlement voting for` AT LEAST `the sum of the unit entitlements` TIMES 50%
                         AND `the lots voting against` LESS THAN `the number of lots in the scheme` TIMES 25%
                         AND `the unit entitlement voting against` LESS THAN `the sum of the unit entitlements` TIMES 25%

§§ `ss 44-47 -- what the by-laws can and cannot do to me`

DECLARE `Kind of by-law` IS ONE OF
    `a governance by-law`   -- Schedule 1 kind: the company's constitution, council, officers, the owner's duties
    `a conduct by-law`      -- Schedule 2 kind: parking, common property, behaviour, rubbish, appearance of the lot

-- s 44(2): "The resolution to make bylaws must be -- (a) for governance bylaws -- a resolution without dissent; and (b) for
-- conduct bylaws -- a special resolution." (3): amending or repealing them takes the same resolution.
-- s 45(2): each person to whom they apply "must comply with the bylaws as if the bylaws were a deed ... containing mutual
-- covenants"; (1)(b) they apply to "a member, for the time being, of the strata company".
DECLARE `What the by-law does` HAS
    `is beyond any power to make it`                                IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 46(a)
    `is inconsistent with the Act or another written law`           IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 46(b)
    `is inconsistent with a restricted use condition`               IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 46(c)
    `denies or limits a member's vote`                              IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 46(e), except as the Act allows
    `restricts selling, leasing, mortgaging or passing on a lot`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 46(f)
    `discharges or modifies an easement or restrictive covenant`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 46(g)
    `restricts an assistance animal of a person with a disability`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 46(h), (i)
    `is unfairly prejudicial, discriminatory, oppressive or unreasonable, as the Tribunal finds` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 46(j): a judgment for the Tribunal

-- s 46: "Scheme bylaws are invalid as follows -- (a) to the extent that there is no power to make the bylaws; (b) ...
-- inconsistent with this Act or any other written law; (c) ... a restricted use condition; ... (e) ... deny or limit the
-- right of a member ... to vote ...; (f) ... prohibit or restrict the devolution of a lot or a transfer, lease, mortgage
-- or other dealing with a lot; (g) ... discharge or modify an easement or restrictive covenant; (h) ... the keeping on a
-- lot of an animal that is used as an assistance animal by a person with a disability ...; (i) ... the use on the parcel
-- of an assistance animal ...; (j) ... (i) unfairly prejudicial to, or unfairly discriminatory against, 1 or more of the
-- owners of lots; or (ii) ... oppressive or unreasonable." s 46(d) (leasehold strata leases) is not encoded.
@export Is this by-law of my strata scheme invalid against me (s 46)?
GIVEN `the by-law` IS A `What the by-law does` @desc What the by-law does, as a set of yes/no facts (the last one is the Tribunal's judgment)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this by-law invalid` IF
        `the by-law`'s `is beyond any power to make it`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `is inconsistent with the Act or another written law`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `is inconsistent with a restricted use condition`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `denies or limits a member's vote`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `restricts selling, leasing, mortgaging or passing on a lot`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `discharges or modifies an easement or restrictive covenant`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `restricts an assistance animal of a person with a disability`
    OR  `the by-law`'s `is unfairly prejudicial, discriminatory, oppressive or unreasonable, as the Tribunal finds`

@export Does this by-law bind me as an owner: was it made by the resolution the Act requires, and is it valid (ss 44(2), 45(2), 46)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of by-law` @desc Whether it is a governance by-law or a conduct by-law
      `it passed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the resolution that made it passed as a special resolution
      `it passed without dissent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the resolution that made it passed as a resolution without dissent (no lot voted against)
      `the by-law` IS A `What the by-law does` @desc What the by-law does, as a set of yes/no facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this by-law bind me` IF
        `it was made by the right resolution`
    AND (NOT `Is this by-law invalid` `the by-law`)
    WHERE
        `it was made by the right resolution` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind`
            WHEN `a governance by-law` THEN `it passed without dissent`
            WHEN `a conduct by-law` THEN `it passed as a special resolution`

-- s 47(2): the strata company's written notice to a person alleged to have contravened the by-laws "must -- (a) specify
-- the particular scheme bylaw ...; (b) specify the particular facts relied on ...; (c) specify the action that must be
-- taken or refrained from ...; and (d) contain an explanation of the effect of this section in terms set out in the
-- regulations" (reg 57: Schedule 2 to the regulations).
@export Is the by-law breach notice the strata company gave me a valid notice (s 47(2); reg 57)?
GIVEN `it names the by-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice specifies the particular by-law said to be broken
      `it states the facts relied on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it specifies the facts relied on as evidence
      `it states what I must do or stop doing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it specifies what you must do or refrain from doing
      `it carries the regulations' explanation of s 47` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it includes the explanation of s 47 in the form of Schedule 2 to the regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the breach notice valid` IF
    `it names the by-law` AND `it states the facts relied on` AND `it states what I must do or stop doing` AND `it carries the regulations' explanation of s 47`

-- s 47(1)(b): the strata company may apply to the Tribunal for an order enforcing the by-laws if "(i) the contravention has
-- had serious adverse consequences for a person other than the person alleged to have contravened ...; or (ii) the person
-- has contravened the particular scheme bylaw on at least 3 separate occasions; or (iii) the person has been given notice
-- under paragraph (a) and has contravened the notice". (3), (4): another owner, a mortgagee or an occupier may apply on the
-- same three grounds.
@export Can the strata company (or another owner or occupier) take me to the Tribunal to enforce a by-law against me (s 47(1)(b), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `it seriously harmed someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the breach had serious adverse consequences for someone other than you
      `the times I have broken that by-law` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many separate occasions you have broken that particular by-law
      `I broke a valid breach notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given a written breach notice under s 47(1)(a) and then contravened it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be taken to the Tribunal over a by-law` IF
        `it seriously harmed someone else`
    OR  `the times I have broken that by-law` AT LEAST 3
    OR  `I broke a valid breach notice`

-- s 47(5)(a): the Tribunal may order the person "pay a specified amount to the strata company by way of penalty"; (6)(c)
-- "the penalty must not exceed an amount fixed by the regulations" ($2 000, reg 58). (8): an amount a member is ordered to
-- pay is recovered, with interest, "as if the amount payable were an unpaid contribution".
@export What is the most the Tribunal can order me to pay as a penalty for breaking a by-law (s 47(6)(c); reg 58), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be made to pay for a by-law breach` IS `the regulated by-law penalty`

@export Can the Tribunal impose a daily penalty on me for a continuing by-law breach (s 47(6)(d))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be given a daily penalty for a by-law breach` IF FALSE

-- s 83: "The owner or occupier of a lot must not use, or permit the use of, the lot or common property ... in a way that
-- interferes unreasonably with the use or enjoyment of another lot or the common property". Whether it is unreasonable is
-- for the Tribunal, so it is an input.
@export Am I in breach of my duty not to interfere unreasonably with other owners' use and enjoyment (s 83)?
GIVEN `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the way you use (or let others use) the lot or common property interferes with someone lawfully using another lot or the common property
      `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interference is unreasonable, as the Tribunal would find
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I breaching the use and enjoyment duty` IF
    `my use interferes with another lot or the common property` AND `the Tribunal would find it unreasonable`

§§ `ss 107, 110 -- the certificate of what is owing`

-- s 107(2): a person with a proper interest includes "(a) a member of the strata company" and "(b) a buyer who has entered
-- into a contract for the sale and purchase of a lot". s 110(2): within 14 days of an application the strata company must
-- certify, for the lot, the contributions determined, "any amount owed ... that is outstanding", and "the rate of interest
-- payable"; penalty for not doing so "a fine of $3 000".
@export What is the most my strata company may charge me for a s 110 certificate about my lot or the scheme (s 107(4); reg 86), in dollars?
GIVEN `the strata company must remit GST for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company is required to remit GST on the fee
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be charged for a certificate` IS
    IF `the strata company must remit GST for it`
    THEN `the regulated certificate fee` TIMES 110%
    ELSE `the regulated certificate fee`

DECLARE `Party to my application` IS ONE OF `the strata company`
DECLARE `Step owed to me` IS ONE OF `give me the s 110 certificate`

@export What is the strata company's duty to give me the s 110 certificate I applied for, and by when (s 110(1), (2))?
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to my application` `Step owed to me`
DECIDE `the strata company's duty to give me the certificate` IS
    PARTY  `the strata company`
    MUST   `give me the s 110 certificate`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the strata company`

@export Within how many days must the strata company give me the s 110 certificate after my application is duly made (s 110(1), (2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I get the certificate` IS 14

§§ `ss 3, 156-164 -- buying a lot`

-- s 156(3), (4): where "(a) the strata titles scheme has not been registered; or (b) the first annual general meeting of the
-- strata company has not been held; or (c) the scheme developer owns 50% or more of the lots ... or lots with an aggregate
-- unit entitlement of 50% or more", and "the scheme developer is the seller", the seller must also give the buyer the
-- estimated income and expenditure for 12 months after settlement, the s 79 disclosures, the services contracts and the
-- leases and licences over common property.
@export As a buyer from the developer, must I also be given the strata company's estimated budget and the developer's contracts and disclosures before I sign (s 156(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the seller is the scheme developer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying from the scheme developer
      `the scheme is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata titles scheme has been registered
      `the first annual general meeting has been held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the strata company's first annual general meeting has been held
      `the developer's share of the lots` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction of the lots the developer owns (for example 0.6)
      `the developer's share of the unit entitlements` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction of the total unit entitlement the developer's lots carry
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the developer give me its extra disclosures` IF
        `the seller is the scheme developer`
    AND (    (NOT `the scheme is registered`)
          OR (NOT `the first annual general meeting has been held`)
          OR `the developer's share of the lots` AT LEAST 50%
          OR `the developer's share of the unit entitlements` AT LEAST 50%)

-- s 3(1): "type 1 notifiable variation means any of the following that occur after a contract ... but before the settlement
-- date -- (a) the area or size of the lot or proposed lot is reduced by 5% or more ...; (b) the proportion that the unit
-- entitlement ... bears to the sum of the unit entitlements of all the lots is increased by 5% or more, or decreased by 5%
-- or more, from the proportion ... notified to the buyer ...; (c) anything relating to a proposal for the termination of
-- the strata titles scheme is served on the seller". "type 2 notifiable variation" -- those "that do not give rise to a
-- type 1 notifiable variation": the scheme plan modified so as to affect the lot or common property; the schedule of unit
-- entitlements modified so as to affect the lot; the by-laws modified; a contract for services or amenities entered or
-- varied; a lease, licence, right or privilege over common property granted or varied. The encoder reads "increased by 5%"
-- as a change of 5% of the notified proportion, not 5 percentage points. Items left to the regulations are not encoded.
DECLARE `Notifiable variation` IS ONE OF
    `a type 1 notifiable variation`
    `a type 2 notifiable variation`
    `no notifiable variation`

DECLARE `What changed before settlement` HAS
    `the notified area of the lot`                     IS A NUMBER    -- square metres told to the buyer before signing
    `the area of the lot now`                          IS A NUMBER
    `the notified unit entitlement`                    IS A NUMBER    -- of the lot, or its reasonable estimate (s 156(2)(b))
    `the notified sum of unit entitlements`            IS A NUMBER
    `the unit entitlement now`                         IS A NUMBER
    `the sum of unit entitlements now`                 IS A NUMBER
    `termination proposal papers were served on the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the scheme plan was modified affecting the lot or common property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the by-laws were modified`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a services contract was entered or varied`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a lease or licence over common property was granted or varied` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Did what changed between my signing and settlement amount to a type 1 or type 2 notifiable variation (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `the change` IS A `What changed before settlement` @desc What changed after you signed the contract and before settlement
GIVETH A `Notifiable variation`
DECIDE `What kind of notifiable variation is it` IS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the area fell by 5% or more`
            OR `the proportion moved by 5% or more`
            OR `the change`'s `termination proposal papers were served on the seller`
            THEN `a type 1 notifiable variation`
        IF     `the change`'s `the scheme plan was modified affecting the lot or common property`
            OR `the unit entitlement schedule changed for the lot`
            OR `the change`'s `the by-laws were modified`
            OR `the change`'s `a services contract was entered or varied`
            OR `the change`'s `a lease or licence over common property was granted or varied`
            THEN `a type 2 notifiable variation`
        OTHERWISE `no notifiable variation`
    WHERE
        `the area fell by 5% or more` MEANS
            `the change`'s `the area of the lot now` AT MOST `the change`'s `the notified area of the lot` TIMES 95%
        `the notified proportion` MEANS
            `the change`'s `the notified unit entitlement` DIVIDED BY `the change`'s `the notified sum of unit entitlements`
        `the proportion now` MEANS
            `the change`'s `the unit entitlement now` DIVIDED BY `the change`'s `the sum of unit entitlements now`
        `the proportion moved by 5% or more` MEANS
                `the proportion now` AT LEAST `the notified proportion` TIMES 105%
            OR  `the proportion now` AT MOST `the notified proportion` TIMES 95%
        `the unit entitlement schedule changed for the lot` MEANS
                (NOT (`the change`'s `the unit entitlement now` EQUALS `the change`'s `the notified unit entitlement`))
            OR  (NOT (`the change`'s `the sum of unit entitlements now` EQUALS `the change`'s `the notified sum of unit entitlements`))

-- s 158(1): "A buyer may, by written notice to the seller, postpone the settlement date ... if the seller has not complied
-- with section 156 or 157." (2): "by no more than 15 working days after the latest date on which the seller complies".
-- s 3(1): "working day means a day other than a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday throughout the State".
@export As a buyer, may I postpone settlement because the seller has not given me the required strata information (s 158)?
GIVEN `the seller complied with s 156` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave you everything s 156 requires before you signed
      `the seller complied with s 157` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller notified every notifiable variation as s 157 requires (true if none occurred)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I postpone settlement` IF
    (NOT `the seller complied with s 156`) OR (NOT `the seller complied with s 157`)

@export If I postpone settlement under s 158, by at most how many working days after the seller finally complies?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many working days may I postpone settlement after compliance` IS 15

-- s 159(1): the buyer may avoid the contract before settlement "(a) if the seller has not complied with section 156; and
-- (b) if the seller were now to comply ..., the buyer would receive information or a document that would disclose material
-- prejudice to the buyer (proof of which lies on the buyer)". (2): if the seller gives a notice substantially complying
-- before the buyer avoids, the buyer may avoid "only if the buyer does so within 15 working days after the seller's notice".
@export As a buyer, may I avoid my contract because the seller did not give me the s 156 information before I signed (s 159)?
GIVEN `the seller complied with s 156` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave you everything s 156 requires before you signed
      `the missing information shows material prejudice to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information not given would disclose material prejudice to you (you must prove it)
      `settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract has already settled
      `the seller has since given substantially complying notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has since given a notice substantially complying with s 156
      `working days since that notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since that late notice was given (0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I avoid for missing disclosure` IF
        (NOT `settlement has happened`)
    AND (NOT `the seller complied with s 156`)
    AND `the missing information shows material prejudice to me`
    AND (    (NOT `the seller has since given substantially complying notice`)
          OR `working days since that notice` AT MOST 15)

-- s 157(3): the seller must notify a notifiable variation "(a) if the seller becomes aware of the notifiable variation less
-- than 15 working days before the settlement date -- as soon as practicable; and (b) in any other case -- not later than 10
-- working days after the seller becomes aware".
-- s 160: the buyer may avoid "within 15 working days after the seller gives the buyer a notice under section 157(1)" if the
-- variation is not one the contract foretold (s 157(4)) and "the buyer is materially prejudiced". s 161: for a type 1
-- variation the seller did not "substantially comply" in time with, the buyer may avoid before settlement, and after a late
-- notice within 15 working days of it. s 162: the same for type 2, but only where the information "would disclose material
-- prejudice to the buyer".
@export As a buyer, may I avoid my contract because of a notifiable variation between signing and settlement (ss 157, 160-162)?
GIVEN `the variation` IS A `Notifiable variation` @desc The kind of notifiable variation that occurred
      `the contract foretold it and it matched` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract described the proposed change and the change as completed matched (s 157(4))
      `the seller notified it in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller gave you notice of it within the time s 157(3) allows
      `the seller has given notice of it at all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has given you notice of the variation at any time
      `working days since the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since that notice was given (0 if none)
      `it materially prejudices me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are materially prejudiced by the variation (you must prove it)
      `settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract has already settled
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I avoid for a notifiable variation` IF
        `under s 160`
    OR  ((NOT `settlement has happened`) AND `under s 161 or s 162`)
    WHERE
        `within 15 working days of any notice` MEANS
            (NOT `the seller has given notice of it at all`) OR `working days since the notice` AT MOST 15
        `under s 160` MEANS
                `the seller has given notice of it at all`
            AND `working days since the notice` AT MOST 15
            AND (NOT `the contract foretold it and it matched`)
            AND `it materially prejudices me`
            AND (NOT (`the variation` EQUALS `no notifiable variation`))
        `under s 161 or s 162` MEANS
            (NOT `the seller notified it in time`) AND `within 15 working days of any notice` AND
            CONSIDER `the variation`
            WHEN `a type 1 notifiable variation` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a type 2 notifiable variation` THEN `it materially prejudices me`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 163(2): a contract for a lot not yet created "must -- (a) require any deposit or other amount payable by the buyer
-- prior to registration ... to be paid ... to a legal practitioner, real estate agent or settlement agent to be held on
-- trust for the buyer until the scheme is registered; and (b) specify the practitioner or agent". (3): the buyer may, "at
-- any time before registration", avoid the contract if "(a) the contract does not comply with subsection (2); or (b) the
-- scheme or amendment is not registered -- (i) within a period after the date of the contract agreed in writing ...; or
-- (ii) in the absence of such an agreement, within 6 months after that date". The encoder counts the period in whole
-- months from the date of the contract (the later signing day, s 163(4)).
@export As a buyer off the plan, may I avoid my contract because the deposit is not held on trust or the scheme is not registered in time (s 163)?
GIVEN `the scheme is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme (or the amendment creating your lot) has been registered
      `the contract has the deposit held on trust by a named practitioner or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract requires the deposit to be held on trust for you by a lawyer, real estate agent or settlement agent it names
      `a period for registration was agreed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the seller agreed in writing on a period for registration
      `the agreed period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that period in months; otherwise 0
      `whole months since the date of the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since the contract was signed (by the last party to sign)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I avoid my off-the-plan contract` IF
        (NOT `the scheme is registered`)
    AND (    (NOT `the contract has the deposit held on trust by a named practitioner or agent`)
          OR `whole months since the date of the contract` AT LEAST `the period`)
    WHERE
        `the period` MEANS
            IF `a period for registration was agreed in writing` THEN `the agreed period in months` ELSE 6

-- s 164(2): on avoidance "(a) the buyer may recover from the seller as a debt all money paid by the buyer under the
-- contract; and (b) a person who is holding a deposit or other amount on behalf of the buyer ... must repay the deposit ...
-- minus any amount due to the seller as rent for any period during which the buyer was in occupation". The encoder reads
-- the rent as coming off the held deposit, and the rest of the money paid as owed by the seller.
@export If I avoid my contract to buy a lot, how much do I get back (s 164(2))?
GIVEN `the deposit held for me` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars held on your behalf as a deposit by an agent or practitioner
      `other money I paid the seller` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other dollars you paid the seller under the contract
      `rent due for my occupation` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars due to the seller as rent for any time you occupied the lot (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much do I get back` IS
    `the deposit held for me` MINUS `rent due for my occupation` PLUS `other money I paid the seller`

§§ `ss 197, 210 -- challenging a decision`

-- s 197(1)(a): scheme disputes between scheme participants (s 197(2)(d): "a member of the strata company") about the scheme
-- documents "including the validity of scheme bylaws", "the performance of, or the failure to perform, a function",
-- "an alleged contravention of this Act (other than an offence)", "a resolution or decision of a strata company or the
-- council ..., including its validity"; (1)(h) a dispute between a buyer and the seller "about a matter arising under Part
-- 10". (3): NOT scheme disputes -- "(c) a dispute with the Valuer-General or a rating or taxing authority; (d) a dispute
-- about a contract of mortgage insurance under section 84; (e) a contractual dispute ... between (i) a scheme participant
-- and a person who is not a scheme participant ...; (f) a dispute about an amount owed as a debt (other than a debt owed
-- under section 99(2) or clause 53E)". (4): a party to the dispute may apply.
DECLARE `My dispute` IS ONE OF
    `the validity of a by-law`
    `a resolution or decision of the strata company or its council`
    `the strata company's failure to perform a function`
    `another owner's contravention of the Act`
    `the seller's disclosure when I bought the lot`
    `how much I owe the strata company as a debt`
    `a contract with a contractor who is not a scheme participant`
    `rates or values set by the Valuer-General or a rating authority`
    `my mortgage insurance contract`

@export Can I, as a lot owner, apply to the State Administrative Tribunal to resolve this dispute as a scheme dispute (s 197)?
GIVEN `the dispute` IS A `My dispute` @desc What the dispute is about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I take this dispute to the Tribunal` IF
    CONSIDER `the dispute`
    WHEN `how much I owe the strata company as a debt` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a contract with a contractor who is not a scheme participant` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `rates or values set by the Valuer-General or a rating authority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `my mortgage insurance contract` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 210(1): where the Tribunal "is constituted without a judicial member and ... makes an order ... of a kind specified in
-- the regulations, a party ... may apply for internal review". reg 162: "an order made by the Tribunal constituted by a
-- member who is not a legally qualified member is specified". (2): only "(a) [if] leave is given by the Tribunal ... and
-- (b) the application is made within 28 days after the order or declaration is made or within an extension of that period
-- given by the President". A member who is not legally qualified is taken to be not a judicial member (inference).
@export Can I apply for internal review of a Tribunal order made in my strata dispute (s 210; reg 162)?
GIVEN `the order was made by a member who is not legally qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal member who made the order is not a legally qualified member
      `the Tribunal gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal gives leave for the internal review
      `days since the order` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the order was made
      `the President extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the President has extended the 28-day period (and you are within it)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I seek internal review` IF
        `the order was made by a member who is not legally qualified`
    AND `the Tribunal gives leave`
    AND (`days since the order` AT MOST 28 OR `the President extended the time`)
